  "ProtoPrecursorIngotEncy_Title": "Alien Modular Framework",
  "ProtoPrecursorIngotEncy_Body": "An advanced material with high structural integrity. Its core, a modified alien building block, stabilizes 8 external frames used for dynamic construction.\n\nAnalysis:\n- Unprecedenteed structural integrity\n- Used in reinforced alien construction\n- Requires multiple advanced materials",
  "ProtoCloakEncy_Title": "Light Distortion Field",
  "ProtoCloakEncy_Body": "This schematic provides missing data used by light refractors lining the hull of the Prototype. The refractors generate a radius around the Prototype whereby external light is dynamically bent around the submarine, making it difficult for aggressive fauna to hit.\n\nIt is clear that the intended use for this technology is to decrease the accuracy of aggressive fauna during emergency scenarios, and the reflective barrier does <b>NOT</b> appear to hinder fauna from initially detecting the Prototype through vibrations and sound.",
  "ProtoEmergencyWarpEncy_Title": "Emergency Warp Protocol",
  "ProtoEmergencyWarpEncy_Body": "This schematic contains a backdoor protocol for the Prototype's archway interceptor which enables it to instantaneously transport the vessel to a pre-specified location; Likely the submarine's point of construction.\n- Due to the immense concentration of dark energy delegated to this protocol, it is likely that all on-board power will be consumed upon using it.",
  "ProtoInterceptorEncy_Title": "UNUSED",
  "ProtoInterceptorEncy_Body": "UNUSED.",
  "ProtoRepairDroidsEncy_Title": "Repair Droids",
  "ProtoRepairDroidsEncy_Body": "This schematic details protocols enabling access to 4 autonomous maintenance robot assembly depots located in the Prototype’s upper stern. Autonomous repair droid construction schematics match data found in background scans of previously-discovered alien facilities.\n\nRepair droids possess advanced welding technology capable of repairing external hull damage over time.\nSafety protocols onboard maintenance robots prevent droid deployment during creature attacks.",
  "ProtoDepthOptimizersEncy_Title": "Depth Optimizers",
  "ProtoDepthOptimizersEncy_Body": "This protocol activates passive depth optimizers built into the hull of the Prototype. These optimizers semi-permanently reinforce the Prototype’s hull, allowing for near unlimited crush depth and greater efficiency at increased depths.",
  "ProtoIonBarrierEncy_Title": "Ion Barrier",
  "ProtoIonBarrierEncy_Body": "This schematic links ion energy emitters lining the hull of the Prototype. The generated energy field creates a thin electrostatic mesh surrounding the vessel capable of absorbing blunt force impacts. The maximum capacity for the energy cells powering the energy emitters is limited, meaning that the barrier may require time to recharge in-between activations and may only fully protect the vessel for a few seconds at a time. The barrier appears to be able to absorb impacts and re-direct their energy back into the Prototype.\n<b>Assessment: Consistent timing allows for power generation through repeated shock absorption</b>",
  "ProtoStasisPulseEncy_Title": "Stasis Pulse",
  "ProtoStasisPulseEncy_Body": "This schematic uses energy emitters lining the hull of the ship to passively collect and discharge electrostatic energy. The discharge of this energy  resembles the latest defensive developments in the <i>Survival-Grade Alterra Stasis Rifle</i>. Upon charge and activation, the electrostatic pulse will temporarily paralyse nearby biological tissues, some internal organs and all brain activity. Paralysis of nearby organisms is dependent on their size; Larger organisms may regain mental functioning faster than smaller ones.\n\n<b>Warning: Experiencing a discharge from this module may semi-permanently damage key cognitive functions such as muscle control, mental clarity and communication from the brain stem to vital and sensory organs causing potential brain death from cerebral hypoxia within 10 minutes of infliction. Avoid at all costs.</b>",
  "ProtoIonGeneratorEncy_Title": "Ion Generator",
  "ProtoIonGeneratorEncy_Body": "By re-routing power from all non-essential systems onboard the Prototype, this module allows the ion reactor to serve as a miniaturized fusion reactor, Slowly regenerating power over time.Due to the extreme conservation of power necessary to carry out the fusion reaction, the following systems are non-functional while the ion generator is active:\n   - Defense modules\n   - Ion thrusters\n\n- If left unsupervised for extended periods of time, there is a significant risk of potentially dangerous gamma radiation buildup.",
  "ProtoOverclockEncy_Title": "Overclock Protocol",
  "ProtoOverclockEncy_Body": "This protocol appears to temporarily sever several safety protocols onboard the Prototype. On activation, the vessel will expend a significant amount of energy to increase power running through the ship’s ion thruster, resulting in an increased speed.",
  "ProtoDeployableLightEncy_Title": "Photon Beacon",
  "ProtoDeployableLightEncy_Body": "This device appears to have been designed either as a navigational and visual aid, or as a decoy for aggressive fauna; perhaps both. Its design accomodates a central exothermic and chemiluminescent reaction suspended between two halves of the device using precise sound waves. The energy contained within this sample is enough to illuminate the device’s surroundings a few hundred meters in each direction, and will last for approximately five minutes.",
  "ProtoIonPrismEncy_Title": "Ion Prism",
  "ProtoIonPrismEncy_Body": "The energy contained within this artefact is significantly higher than any previously-encountered alien power source. If released, the resulting thermonuclear explosion would reach a distance of approximately 50 kilometers and would prove fatal to all biological life within the crater. In its current state, it does not seem possible nor wise to attempt to extract the energy from its container. Therefore, in order to use this object to power equipment, currently undiscovered technology would be needed.\n\n<b>Assessment: Handle with utmost care</b>",
  "OrionFacilityLogs_Title": "Maternal Megafauna Aggression Research Data",
  "OrionFacilityLogs_Body": "According to translated data logs, this facility was constructed to develop defensive technologies for the alien dead zone mapping initiative. These technologies were designed to protect a vessel of a similar description to the one previously-constructed at the Quarantine Enforcement Platform, albeit with distinct differences in its on-board AI systems, against leviathan-class lifeforms inhabiting the ecological dead zone surrounding the crater.\n\nHowever, a more recent development in this facility’s directives follows a command issued by an executive member of the alien hierarchy involving leviathan-class embryo study for the bacterium research project, of which the dead zone mapping initiative is a subsidiary. this facility’s primary directive was to research and document the aggressive behaviours of a leviathan-class organisms in order to ensure the safety of the bacterium research facility in its own analytic endeavours. Following this command, this facility began preparations to collect a leviathan-class egg sample and study the aggressive behaviours of the egg’s parent in a controlled environment. This project’s data file is interrupted by a lockdown procedure during this phase, however, and no results are present within the following logs.",
  "DefenseFacilityLogs_Title": "Defense Facility Lockdown Procedure",
  "DefenseFacilityLogs_Body": "This terminal appears to have been controlling the parameters surrounding this facility’s lockdown procedure which used several advanced technologies to fully protect the facility's sensitive data.\nTo protect the facility from megafauna attacks, the aliens used a light distortion field, an ionic barrier system, an electrostatic pulse emitter as well as a massive physical barrier. The facility itself was also placed in a highly defensible location between two abyssal cliff faces.\nThe facility's lockdown order was given by an impromptu command issued within the alien bacterium research facility after a catastrophic structural collapse caused an outbreak of a foreign bacterium into the planet's ecosystem.\n- The final audit message indicates that this lockdown was lifted mere seconds ago.",
  "EngineFacilityLogs_Title": "Ion Reactor Testing Facility Audit Logs",
  "EngineFacilityLogs_Body": "The following audit log outlines the operational data output from this facility dating back approximately 1000 years. Data relating to specific chronological periods is unable to be translated. However, the order of events has been preserved:\n\n┃▚╋▚┗     Facility established, stored thermal energy increasing.\n▜┏┃┃▖       Beginning ion reactor stress diagnostics.\n▙▞┏┃       Interplanetary vessel detected within quarantine zone.\n▜▞╋▚       Energy discharge detected in Quarantine Enforcement Platform. Re-routing power. Warning: Prototype energy infrastructure failing.\n┅┏┫           Entering hibernation. Stored energy: 0 ▟\n▙┏┻┃             Audit log retrieved.",
  "ProtoDatabankEncy_Title": "Prototype Vessel Schematic",
  "ProtoDatabankEncy_Body": "The data transmitted from this terminal outlines schematics for a large, highly robust sub-aquatic vessel used to collect geographical data from bodies of water at great depths. Evidence suggests the vessel is missing several of its core functions.\n\nThe schematic description includes:\n- A default crush depth of 600 meters.\n- Terrain-scanning technology somewhat resembling human sonar equipment\n- A large, hull-piercing intrusion situated at the vessel’s core, potentially indicating corrupted exterior schematics\n- 3 floors of useable interior\n- A launch bay used to deploy various single-use devices\n- A highly advanced fusion reactor capable of harboring and routing ion energy\n\nBased on these schematics, it may be possible to assemble upgrades to improve the vessel’s crush depth, speed and unique abilities through interaction with other alien data terminals. The Alterra corporation advises that this data be uploaded immediately to the nearest trans-gov mandated data terminal to ensure the safe collection of all potentially dangerous alien da--\n\n<b>┛▖▛▚┣┅ protocols activated. Severing data stream.</b>",
  "ProtoFacilitiesEncy_Title": "Prototype Project Facilities",
  "ProtoFacilitiesEncy_Body": "Four alien facilities have been identified in reference to the alien “Dead zone mapping initative”. Each facility appears to be dedicated to developing technologies for a specific aspect of the Prototype.\n\nIon Reactor Testing Facility:\n- Depth: 460m\n- Location: Inside a large outcropping at the outer edge of a large, dark region 1 kilometer west-northwest of the Enforcement Platform.\n- Objective: Maintain access to Prototype development facilities via ion energy delegation.\n<b>Objective failed</b>\n\nWarp Technologies Development Facility:\n- Depth: 700m\n- Location: Richly bioluminescent cave system below the Quarantine Enforcement Platform\n- Objective: Prevent the spread of Warp Core dark energy.\n<b>Objective failing; Facility inaccessible</b>\n\nDefensive Technologies Research Facility:\n- Depth: 480m\n- Location: Situated between abyssal cliff faces south of the Aurora’s thrusters.\n- Objective: Continue research on maternal megafauna aggression\n<b>Objective overruled; Facility inaccessible</b>\n\nPrototype Administrative Facility:\n- Depth: ▛╋▝▙┗▙\n- Location: ┛┏┫┣▝ ┏▛ ┛▝▞┓\nObjective: ━▖▞┃┣▖▞┃ ▛▖▘▞▄▞┣┅ ▄┏▘▀▙┏┻┃\n<b>Objective met</b>",
  "OrionFragmentorEncy_Title": "Alien Surgical Structure",
  "OrionFragmentorEncy_Body": "This structure vaguely resembles human surgical operating tables, particularly those employing Magnetic Resonance Imaging technology, otherwise known as MRIs.\nScans indicate the two claw-like devices on each side of the table store electrostatic energy similar to those encountered in the Prototype defense facility’s stasis pulse generators, suggesting they may have been used to immobilize the patient during the procedure.\n\nThe uppermost claw contains powerful electromagnets, suggesting that the structure may have been used to scan neural activity, or otherwise extract it. Despite its small size, this structure contains enormous capacity for data transfer, and is in many ways technologically superior to other alien devices encountered thus far, suggesting that its assembly was either a large-scale collaborative effort, or that its creator was particularly specialized in brain scanning technology.\n\n ",
  "HullFacilityLogsEncy_Title": "Prototype Facility Records",
  "HullFacilityLogsEncy_Body": "This terminal contains data corresponding to alien researchers posted within the Prototype administrative facility. The dataset is hugely complex, but some key information can be extracted regarding a total of 6 members of the alien species.\n\n┏▘┣┏\nDiscipline: Prototype project administrator\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Omega\n\n▙▚▖━┏┇\nDiscipline: Mechanical division\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Theta\n\n▄┅┏┃▞▘\nDiscipline: Resources management\nStatus: Deceased\n\n▞┃▙▞▜┏\nDiscipline: Technological research\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Gamma\n\n┏┗▞┏┃\nDiscipline: Robotics development\nStatus: Presumed deceased\n\n▘▄┫▗\nDiscipline: Non-essential systems maintenance\nStatus: Deceased",
  "OrionEndeavorsEncy_Title": "Or-Ion Analytic Endeavors",
  "OrionEndeavorsEncy_Body": "This terminal contains data stored in an audit log format detailing the analytic achievements of a particular member of the alien species automatically translated to Or-Ion.\n\nWas grown from seed approximately 2,000 earth years ago\nWas inducted into temple of research at age 130 after showing early promise in the field of neural analysis and robotics\nRelocated to 4546B to aid in high priority planetary geographical research “Prototype vessel development”\nIndependently invented design for quadrupedal maintenance robot modelled after native 4546B species “Cave Crawler” which was quickly adopted throughout the outer galaxy cluster as precautionary measure\nLed development of natural resource collection tunnel boring device modelled after native 4546B species “Ice Worm” in aid of Prototype development and disease research endeavors\nReceived multiple disciplinary infraction warnings from Prototype project administrator for tampering with robots during operation\nWaived right to enter sanctuary hibernation. Reason: Unfinished work",
  "AlienBuildingBlockEncy_Title": "Alien Building Block",
  "AlienBuildingBlockEncy_Body": "This terminal outlines key characteristics of a fundamental resource used in the construction of alien architecture and technology. The alien 'building block' is reported to contain both cybernetic and biological elements, and is used in a wide range of alien technologies.\n\nA disclaimer at the summary of the info sheet reads:\n'Energy systems in self-warping constructs require perpetual building block consumption. Constructs are programmed to expel discharged building blocks marked with a pulsating yellow glow rechargeable by any multi-use fabrication terminal upon using warping technology.'\n\nBased on this message, it may be possible to acquire discharged building blocks from still-functional warper constructs or from the ground surrounding them and use the remnant to fabricate alien resources.\n\n<b>Assessment: The Alterra corporation is not responsible for bodily harm caused by failed attempts to retrieve this object from self-warping constructs.</b>",
  "HullFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Prototype Administrative Tablet",
  "HullFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "This alien tablet hums with a constant stream of low-level ionic pulses, possibly as a form of location tracking or clearance detection. This suggests the tablet is of a higher security class than previously discovered alien tablets. The central black symbol resembles the previously encountered symbol for the alien Prototype vessel project, suggesting that it was developed to manage security clearance solely for individuals working on it.",
  "EngineFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Ion Facility Tablet",
  "EngineFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Downloaded from a local broadcast in the Quarantine Enforcement Platform, this alien tablet features a prominent triangular symbol at its centre and passively radiates at an intensity of 70mSv. The tablet itself contains traces of ionic energy similar to those contained within traditional alien power sources. While it is unclear what use the tablet may have served, it may have been used as a temporary store of ionic energy for technological development, or as a fuse-like safety device.",
  "InterceptorFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Interceptor Facility Tablet",
  "InterceptorFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Compiled from data pertaining to the Prototype's archway teleportation systems, this alien device is emblazoned with a purple symbol bearing a resemblance to previously-encountered alien archways. The symbol itself appears to contain trace levels of dormant antimatter particles. \nWhile the device's purpose is unclear, potential applications may include:\n- An antimatter storage device\n- A device used to test advanced alien transportation\n- A personal short-range alien transportation device",
  "DefenseFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Defense Facility Tablet",
  "DefenseFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Compiled from data pertaining to the Prototype's defensive systems, this alien tablet bears a red octagonal symbol, possibly representing stability or protection. The core of this alien tablet measures a total of 200 degrees Celcius. While it is unclear what purpose this may serve, it is possible that the aliens used temperature as a form of “tag” with which to classify their artifacts.",
  "ProtoWarpReactorEncy_Title": "Warp Core",
  "ProtoWarpReactorEncy_Body": "This alien artifact, taking the shape of a square bipyramid, appears to be harbouring massive amounts of concentrated dark energy not entirely dissimilar to the kind found within the Aurora’s dark matter reactor. Due to this kind of energy being primarily used for transportation and interdimensional matter translation across vast distances, it is reasonable to assume that this artefact may be a kind of ‘battery’ containing energy used by the alien species for different manners of teleportation.\n\n<b>Protective Shields</b>\n\n8 pyramid-shaped energy barriers surround the central warp core. These barriers are exhibiting substantial signs of decay as dark matter radiates from the core between them. It is clear that these shields have been built to withstand extreme levels of quantum dissonance, but that these levels may have gone unregulated for long enough to cause the protective shields to falter and release a sudden impulse of concentrated dark energy.\n\n<b>Surrounding Structure</b>\n\nThe surrounding structure also appears to be suffering from degradation caused by the leaking dark energy from the central core, leading to visible cracks and momentary pulses of dark energy through the structure.\n\n<b>Assessment: Highly unstable levels of dark energy present; Proceed with caution\n",
  
  "ProtoWormEncy_Title": "Wyrm Xenoleviathan (Operational)",
  "ProtoWormEncy_Body": "A highly advanced tool, this robotic specimen is capable of large-scale resource extraction and subterranean self-navigation. It does not exhibit any directly aggressive tendencies. However, due the high concentration of rare minerals in Alterra technology, it may still pose a substantial threat to submersible hull integrity and overall safety if it deems such technology worth extracting.\n\n1. Mineral extraction equipment:\nThis autonomous device is equipped with highly advanced material extraction technologies. A frontal set of rotating frames exceeding 1,500 degrees Celcius serve to melt the outer layers of bedrock and minerals before passing them down through the specimen's body.\n\n2. Material transportation:\nThe “spine” of the specimen controls a powerful beam of a plasma-like substance which directs the flow of liquid mineral resources, distributing it throughout each spine segment which slowly fill with raw minerals as the wyrm moves through the ground.\n\n3. Profile:\nThe specimen measures a total of 220 metres in length. It appears to disregard the presence of living fauna, suggesting purely practical applications. Because the Alterra Corporation has not published specifications regarding the class assignment “leviathan” to cybernetic or robotic phenomena, this PDA will assign this specimen the class designation Xenoleviathan. Upon re-entry to trans-gov mandated space, data pertaining to this phenomena will undergo investigation from Alterra HQ and an official designation proclamation surrounding the specimen will be made.\n\n<b>Assessment:  Remain vigilant for subterranean boring in deeper regions.</b>",
  "ProtoHangingWormEncy_Title": "Alien Wyrm (Modified)",
  "ProtoHangingWormEncy_Body": "This alien wyrm appears to be a slightly modified version of previously-encountered models. Noteworthy modifications include an appended seed code marked, to some extent, for influence within this facility, likely as a precautionary measure only extended to this particular wyrm specimen for unknown reasons. Additionally, the body of the wyrm has been largely protected by the surrounding terrain, resulting in comparitively high remaining structural integrity compared to other models.\n\n<b>Assessment: May be scavenged for valuable material extraction equipment. Further investigation required.</b>",
  "ProtoDecorativeWormEncy_Title": "Alien Wyrm (Dysfunctional)",
  "ProtoDecorativeWormEncy_Body": "This colossal device is of alien origin, though is likely either unpowered or malfunctioning.\n\nRadio network:\nThe device is connected to several others like it through a radio channel, as well as to a central operations facility located far beneath it. While the device is unable to transmit signals, it is ‘listening’ for a signal from a specific source.\n\nFunction and threat assessment:\nWhile the exact function of this device is unclear, its foremost segment is designed either to cut, melt or otherwise dissolve rocks and minerals. This suggests that the device was used to collect such resources from layers of upper bedrock found in regions exceeding 200m in depth.\n\n<b>Assessment: May prove hazardous while functioning; Do not attempt to re-activate</b>",
  "HullFacilityWormTerminalEncy_Title": "Dead Zone Mapping Initiative Project Data",
  "HullFacilityWormTerminalEncy_Body": "According to translated administrative logs, the dead zone mapping initiative, a subsidiary of the bacterium research project, was enacted to supplement a design limitation in the aliens’ existing satellite technology: Depth.\n\nIn an effort to broaden their search for a viable cure to the Khaara bacterium, the aliens began the development of a vessel capable of handling near infinite external pressure and autonomous self-sufficiency. Four facilities were constructed, each developing one aspect of the vessel’s abilities. The ion reactor allowed the vessel to infinitely recharge using external pressure, the archway interceptor used a network of dark energy sources to precisely geolocate at great depths, the vessel’s defensive measures allowed for protection against leviathan-class lifeforms, and the culmination of these branches’ research was assembled in the Prototype Administrative Facility.\n\nHowever, unforeseen circumstances in the bacterium research project forced the dead zone mapping initiative to cease production of the vessel, and its researchers to abandon the project. \n\nBased on this log, it is unclear how the Prototype now stands. However, the term “Natural Selection Program” is repeatedly mentioned during the abandonment of the initiative by its researchers, for unknown reasons.",
  "ProtoAggressiveWyrmEncy_Title": "Wyrm Xenoleviathan (Aggressive)",
  "ProtoAggressiveWyrmEncy_Body": "An unstoppable force of alien technological advancement, this specimen of Wyrm Xenoleviathan is capable of completely decimating both living and nonliving matter at will.\n\n1. Sight Through Chemical Composition\nWhile it posesses no light or heat sensors, its use in underground excavation results in the Wyrm having a keen sense of chemical composition across vast distances- Hiding from it is virtually impossible.\n\n2. Ion Cannon\nAfter locking onto its target, the Wyrm can discharge a devastating burst of energy dissolving anything in its path. However, it may be possible to reflect the shot if a strong enough shield is used against it.\n\n3. Targeted Hostility\nWhile it is unclear why this Wyrm Xenoleviathan is exhibiting aggressive behaviours, it is clear that it is directly targeting you in doing so. As the Wyrm’s aggression subsides when returning from the ecological dead zone, it is possible that it is following a directive created specifically to prevent you from leaving the crater. Reason unknown.\n\n<b>Assessment: Extreme threat. Avoid crater edge at all costs.</b>",
  "FragmentationTerminalEncy_Title": "Neural Cluster Fragmentation Journal",
  "FragmentationTerminalEncy_Body": "Data from this terminal is stored in a journal-like format. Only the most recent entry is immediately available, and appears to have been written by one member of the alien species. The translated entry reads as follows:\n\n“Internal animate entropy is reaching critically low levels. Minimum required concentration for fragmentation remains unclear, despite continued efforts. Treatment will continue on schedule. The resource collection network has been placed on standby. The NSP dictates an eventual re-activation of the selected construct, by which time fragmentation will have long been completed. The predicted animate entropy vessel will encounter this terminal if it is compatible. As I send my regards, I remind it: It cannot fail.”",
  "AnimateEntropyTerminalEncy_Title": "Animate Entropy Cultivation",
  "AnimateEntropyTerminalEncy_Body": "According to translated data logs, this environment was designed to imitate the natural growth conditions for a resource referred to as “animate entropy”, which is reported to have been of critical importance in the harvesting of dark energy and was reportedly discovered by a robotics researcher in the Prototype Administrative Facility.\n\nAs such, this facility was likely used to naturally cultivate animate entropy for the research of miniaturized warp technologies through dark matter manipulation. This research appears to have, at one point, been delegated to both self-warping constructs and the “dead zone mapping initiative”, but was later consolidated into self-warping construct production following the closure of the latter project.\n\nA seemingly unused data point mentions the application of animate entropy to something referred to as the “NSP”. However, no further data can be construed as to what this project may have entailed.",
  "DefenseFacilityWallEncy_Title": "Facility Barrier",
  "DefenseFacilityWallEncy_Body": "This barrier is composed of a heavily reinforced alloy of several alien materials. Its position suggests that it was created to protect the central hub from leviathan attacks. Several large shock-absorbing panels suggests the barrier was also used to record and gather data on the forces, patterns and behaviours of different leviathan attacks.\n\nIt is unclear how leviathan-class lifeforms may have been encouraged to attack the facility within as scans of the barrier's integrity show no signs recent impacts.",
  
  "ProtoFins_Title": "Prototype Fins",
  "ProtoFins_Body": "These magnetically-controlled implements serve as both structural and propulsory augmentations to the Prototype’s hull. They appear to be fabricated in pairs, and schematic extrapolation indicates a maximum capacity of 4 total pairs of fins.\n\n<b>Structural support</b>\nThese fins act as storage devices for a liquid resource closely resembling the composition of alien facility architecture. While it is unclear how this liquid is extracted, it is used to coat the vessel in a thin layer of reinforcement as external water pressure rises, thereby increasing the maximum crush depth of the vessel. Each individual fin contains enough fluid to increase the Prototype’s maximum crush depth by approximately 175 meters.\n\n<b>Propulsion</b>\nSmall energy receptors lining each fin acts as a siphon to extract energy from the Prototype’s ion reactor. This energy is then channeled into propulsive thrusters located at the bottom of each fin to increase maximum speed by 0.15m/s.",
  "ProtoBuildTerminal_Title": "Construction Terminal",
  "ProtoBuildTerminal_Body": "This device seems to be the origin of the recently-detected neural analysis. Thankfully, the device has been calibrated only to read neural data, and not to write it.\n\nThe device itself appears to serve two primary functions.\n\n1. Data storage:\nThe device harbours a form of algorithmic software referred to as a neural cluster suspended between its upper and lower halves. The neural cluster is marked with seed code “Orion”, a name typically reserved for the famous earth constellation, but that may be a universal identifier. In this case, it is being used possibly as a project title or specimen identification.\n\nThe device is being constantly fed large amounts of highly encrypted data from an unnamed source, likely an off-planet database. The data follows a fractal-like organizational pattern, suggesting infinite possible situational data under infinitely increasing conditions, allowing the terminal to adapt to situational factors in real-time.\n\n2. Vessel construction:\nThe two structures to either side of the terminal appear to be energy storage devices designed to passively gather and quickly discharge large bursts of energy to the central terminal. The drones hovering around the terminal seem to be used to transmit matter. This indicates that the terminal may be used as a fabrication station for a piece of alien technology. Given its position beside an enclosed moonpool, this technology is likely subaquatic in nature.\n\n<b>Assessment: Further research required.</b>",
  "PrecursorSuitTerminalEncy_Title": "Ion Dive Suit Schematic",
  "PrecursorSuitTerminalEncy_Body": "This alien terminal has broadcasted a unique schematic for a piece of alien equipment, adapted for the use of 'Transmission candidate #2'. The schematic draws anatomical data from the Alterra All-Environment Protection Suit, and has modified it with several key features:\n\n1. Biomechanical Energy Storage\nIn order to function properly, the Ion Dive Suit requires an input of alien biomechanical energy through Alien Building Blocks. Once charged, the suit stores this energy and discharges it in a number of different ways.\n\n2. Alien Factors\nThe suit is designed to intake modular upgrades called Factors, each of which are designed to mimic an aspect of the aliens' abilities. Examples include improved environmental resistance, time dilation, teleportation and the ability to 'hear' alien technology when in range.\n\n<b>Assessment: Invaluable technology. Return data to Alterra for mutual profit.</b>",
  "BiomechanicsFactorTerminalEncy_Title": "Woah, title!",
